            <ArticleTitle>Transition-metal-free controlled polymerization for poly(p-aryleneethynylene)s.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>492-496</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c4sc02872d</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A transition-metal-free controlled polymerization for the attainment of poly(p-aryleneethynylene)s is developed. The polymerization of 1-pentafluorophenyl-4-[(trimethylsilyl)ethynyl]benzene with a catalytic amount of fluoride anions proceeds in a chain-growth-like manner to afford polymers with controlled molecular weights and low polydispersity indexes. The mechanism involves a pentacoordinated fluorosilicate as a key intermediate. The anionic &quot;living&quot; nature of this process is applied to block copolymerization and also surface-terminated polymerization.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
